{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c4bb","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0761f-a1d7-7f21-bbcd-d353d9bc9dd9"},"sequence":184,"recorded_at":1780531400000363,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"357b4990-0035-4254-a95a-ceb9ed1d0622","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"357b4990-0035-4254-a95a-ceb9ed1d0622","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"357b4990-0035-4254-a95a-ceb9ed1d0622"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"3b99dafb-d0b8-4356-a719-1f1c80cb266d"},"task_id":"3b99dafb-d0b8-4356-a719-1f1c80cb266d","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"3b99dafb-d0b8-4356-a719-1f1c80cb266d","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-9-1\",\n  \"command\": \"git diff --cached --stat; echo \\\"===\\\"; git diff --cached | head -n 200; echo \\\"===UNSTAGED===\\\"; git diff | head -n 100\",\n  \"description\": \"Inspect staged revert details\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \" LOGBOOK.md                                        |  21 -----\\n README.md                                         |  34 +-------\\n internal/traceability/cmd/tracecheck/main_test.go |   4 +-\\n internal/traceability/ownership.v0.5.0.json       | 102 ----------------------\\n internal/traceability/traceability.go             |   2 +-\\n internal/traceability/traceability_test.go        |   2 +-\\n 6 files changed, 5 insertions(+), 160 deletions(-)\\n===\\ndiff --git a/LOGBOOK.md b/LOGBOOK.md\\nindex fd2a806..dfd0437 100644\\n--- a/LOGBOOK.md\\n+++ b/LOGBOOK.md\\n@@ -5,27 +5,6 @@\\n \\n ## 2026-09-06\\n \\n-### 1035 — Directory-node leaf round-2 rework: rev1 B1/B2/B3 closed, 185-mutant battery\\n-\\n-- SCOPE: TASK-260830-ljkj8r round-2 rework (review-verdict-rev1, changes requested, B1–B3 blocking). Test-only additions inside `internal/dirnode/` (`bound_census_test.go`, `bounds_edge_test.go`, `query_operations_test.go`, `arm_identity_test.go`) plus four one-line fixture-surgery fixes (`query_test.go` unknown_field + missing caller, `manifest_test.go` missing member, `probe_test.go` missing member) and three edge extensions (findings 4097, cursor 1/1024 admission, projection bound edges). No production behavior change. Uncommitted per the CR-shape instruction.\\n-- FIX (B1): bound census ported from the sessadapter leaf — 101 production-derived sites (9 helpers + len/length-var guards, 10-shape space with 6 derived + 4 stated), 72 driven + 29 exempt mechanism/plumbing. Edge drivers prove min-1/min/max/max+1 through the production entry. Battery: 185 applied / 142 behavioural kills / 43 equivalent-with-bound / 0 survivors, zero not-applied, zero compile failures. Census-only kills scored separately (2 live census mutants + 3 synthetic gate proofs).\\n-- FIX (B2): `TestDecodeQueryAllOperationsAdmit` drives 17/17 registry operations (was 5/17); 40+ validator defects through DecodeQuery including the review probes environments/\\\"root\\\", jobs/\\\"pwned\\\", distinct/\\\"secret\\\" (battery V01–V03, all killed). Zero functions at 0.0% (was 10, all §10.8.5 validators).\\n-- FIX (B3): unknown_field rebuilt without the duplicate member + reachability proof; audit found the same rename-instead-of-delete slide in three more missing vectors, all fixed to deletions + message-identity proof. Protocol relabeled-major placeholder verified genuine (overridden with a real relabeled frame).\\n-- FINDINGS: (1) Closed vocabularies mask bound narrowings — 11 count ceilings equal their vocabulary size (no ceiling+1 member buildable) and 20 element bounds cannot discriminate behind the outer gate; all recorded as equivalents, never survivors. (2) Count/index gates coincide at the 65th operation — each single weakening is masked behind the other; pinned jointly. (3) Test scaffolds must not size probes from production constants: the frame suite initially referenced MaxFrameBytes and went green under a widened constant; now retyped (frameBoundBytes) like all fixtures. Same fix applied to two protocol oversize vectors and the uint53 ceiling probe.\\n-- EVIDENCE: attached TASK-260830-ljkj8r_round2.md (verdicts, equivalence classes, full 185-row table, 9/9 AC mapping). Production files byte-identical (battery is copy-back per mutant; post-run grep for mutant literals clean).\\n-- GATES: `go test ./... -count=1` exit 0 (18 pkgs), `-race` on dirnode exit 0, `go vet ./...` and `GOOS=windows go vet ./...` exit 0, gofmt clean, `tracecheck` exit 0 (acceptance_cases=94, unchanged). Dirnode cover 74.9% → 83.3%.\\n-- STATUS: Ready for review, handed off uncommitted.\\n-\\n-### 0930 — Directory-node leaf: `internal/dirnode` implemented with enumerated census first\\n-\\n-- SCOPE: TASK-260830-ljkj8r (second leaf of STORY-260830-3drr2m). New package `internal/dirnode`: two-major manifest bootstrap, envelope framing, manifest/probe/scan/Directory-Query framing, façade host checks, Structured Error 1.2.0 refusals. Six traceability rows (88 → 94), README paragraph. Uncommitted per the CR-shape instruction.\\n-- CENSUS FIRST: the leaf-1 lesson (seven rounds, one repeating mistake class) is applied before the battery, not after. `census_test.go` enumerates 10 of 10 AST shapes carrying an error construction (literal, binary-expr with rendered key, constructor registration, New-outside-body, New-as-value, ctor alias in every position, closure-hidden call, aliased import, frameFault literal) with synthetic proofs and named residue. Result: 147 derived arms (145 witnessed + 2 defensive), 8 constructors. The census caught 5 missing witness rows and 3 vacuous fixture vectors during authoring.\\n-- NO-OP-PROOF VECTORS: every fixture-surgery site uses `replaceOnce`, which fails when the needle is absent — a mutation that changes nothing can no longer pass against a still-valid body.\\n-- FINDINGS: (1) §10.8.5 prose names `query_cursor_mismatch` but the pinned error registry does not register it — cursor reuse refuses as `query_invalid` with a cursor-mismatch detail. (2) The response envelope carries its own `schema` + `schema_version` (1.0.0 both majors): the downgrade tuple names a response schema_version no schemaless reading can carry. (3) `node manifest is not canonical JSON` is reachable, not defensive: extensions values cross opaquely while the canonicalizer enforces depth 256 (300-deep vector proves it). (4) `failCapability` removed — no entry point in this deliverable raises `capability_unavailable`; the taxonomy test pins the 8 emitted codes instead of keeping a dead constructor for census symmetry.\\n-- EVIDENCE: narrowing-mutant battery M1–M8, all killed, 0 survivors (M1 downgrade-retryable, M2 v1-macos, M3 conditional-upgrade, M4 scan-replay, M5 index-contiguity, M6 relabeled-schema-version, M7 reasonless-capability, M8 aliased-import with full behavioral suite green). Every mutant copy-aside/copy-back with `cmp` clean; exit codes unpiped. Census-only kills (M8's 4) scored separately.\\n-- GATES: `go test ./... -count=1` exit 0 (18 pkgs), `-count=3` and `-race` on dirnode exit 0, `-race` on traceability+tracecheck exit 0, `go vet ./...` and `GOOS=windows go vet ./...` exit 0, gofmt clean, `tracecheck` exit 0 (acceptance_cases=94). Full-repo `-race` not run (exceeds one bounded call; raced every touched package instead). Dirnode cover 75.0%.\\n-- STATUS: Ready for review, handed off uncommitted.\\n-\\n ### 0618 — Session-adapter leaf round-4 rework: rev3 B4/B5/B6 closed as classes, N6 fixed in code\\n \\n - SCOPE: TASK-260830-2z3se0 round-4 rework (review-verdict-rev3, changes requested, B4–B6 blocking + N6). Test-only additions inside `internal/sessadapter/` (`zero_absent_test.go`, `bounds_edge_test.go`, `import_census_test.go`) plus a two-line production-test fix in `inventory_test.go` and this entry. No production behavior change; the 323-arm inventory floor is untouched. Uncommitted per the CR-shape instruction.\\ndiff --git a/README.md b/README.md\\nindex 3893b0d..d19c0a8 100644\\n--- a/README.md\\n+++ b/README.md\\n@@ -1987,7 +1987,7 @@ go test ./internal/catalog ./internal/cataloggen ./internal/catalog/cmd/catalogg\\n repository gate used by CI. Its reviewed\\n [`ownership.v0.5.0.json`](internal/traceability/ownership.v0.5.0.json)\\n registry independently enumerates implementation owners for all 60 current\\n-contract rows, 36 pinned or catalog-referenced normative section keys, 94\\n+contract rows, 36 pinned or catalog-referenced normative section keys, 88\\n executable acceptance cases, 53 exact section bindings with their declared\\n coverage, 2 disclosed unowned sections, and 30 exact fixture identities or\\n Appendix D anchors. The v0.4.3 projection is checked as an owned 55-contract subset.\\n@@ -2176,38 +2176,6 @@ positive and refusal tests. The Section 7.8 clause-level binding stays\\n against an acceptance case, so the registry makes no clause-level claim\\n about the obligations it carries.\\n \\n-The Directory Node host surface lives in\\n-[`internal/dirnode`](internal/dirnode): the two-major manifest\\n-bootstrap (`DecideBootstrapStep` with its exact downgrade tuple,\\n-`ProcessGuard`, `NextLowerMajor`), request/response envelope\\n-framing (`EncodeRequest`, `DecodeRequestFrame`,\\n-`CheckSuccessEnvelope`, `CheckFailureEnvelope`), manifest decoding\\n-with façade binding checks (`DecodeManifest`,\\n-`CheckManifestBindings`, `AvailableCapabilities`), per-major probe\\n-framing with the node-build equality gate (`CheckProbeRequest`,\\n-`CheckProbeResponse`, `CheckNodeBuildEqualsManifest`), scan\\n-framing with the `(operation, operation_id)` idempotency journal\\n-and its crash-recovery export/import (`CheckScanRequest`,\\n-`CheckScanResponse`, `Journal`), and Session Directory Query\\n-framing (`DecodeQuery`, `CheckCursorReuse`). Six executable\\n-acceptance cases (`directory-node-bootstrap`,\\n-`directory-node-manifest`, `directory-node-probe`,\\n-`directory-node-scan`, `directory-node-query`,\\n-`directory-node-idempotency`) bind those entry points to their\\n-named positive and refusal tests, and an AST-derived refusal-arm\\n-inventory (`census_test.go`) requires every production refusal arm\\n-— literal, fault-detail conduit, and branch-prefix expression\\n-shapes — to resolve to a named asserting test in both directions,\\n-with two recorded defensive arms that no public input can fire.\\n-The Section 7.9 clause-level binding stays `unevidenced` (catalog\\n-`ForRelease` only): no clause of 7.9 is enumerated against an\\n-acceptance case, so the registry makes no clause-level claim\\n-about the obligations it carries. The framed subset is exactly\\n-manifest, probe, and scan plus the Directory Query contract; the\\n-remaining eight registry operations carry nested content owned by\\n-the sibling leaves and are pinned as unframed by\\n-`TestFramedSubsetIsExact`, not silently absent.\\n-\\n Successful output reports ownership inventory counts and the measured coverage\\n ratio only. The gate does not mutate repository or product state, add an `ax`\\n command or `doctor` result, or claim that any catalog capability is available,\\ndiff --git a/internal/traceability/cmd/tracecheck/main_test.go b/internal/traceability/cmd/tracecheck/main_test.go\\nindex 8ffceba..506e9a1 100644\\n--- a/internal/traceability/cmd/tracecheck/main_test.go\\n+++ b/internal/traceability/cmd/tracecheck/main_test.go\\n@@ -22,7 +22,7 @@ func TestRunReportsExactCoverageAndFailsClosed(t *testing.T) {\\n \\tif err := run([]string{\\\"-root\\\", repositoryRoot}, &output); err != nil {\\n \\t\\tt.Fatalf(\\\"run() error = %v\\\", err)\\n \\t}\\n-\\twant := \\\"traceability ok: contracts=60 normative_sections=36 acceptance_cases=94 fixtures=30 compatibility_contracts=55 assigned_scopes=0\\\\n\\\" +\\n+\\twant := \\\"traceability ok: contracts=60 normative_sections=36 acceptance_cases=88 fixtures=30 compatibility_contracts=55 assigned_scopes=0\\\\n\\\" +\\n \\t\\t\\\"section coverage: bindings=53 full=1 partial=3 sliver