{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c653","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0761f-a1d7-7f21-bbcd-d353d9bc9dd9"},"sequence":388,"recorded_at":1780531400000771,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"357b4990-0035-4254-a95a-ceb9ed1d0622","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"357b4990-0035-4254-a95a-ceb9ed1d0622","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"357b4990-0035-4254-a95a-ceb9ed1d0622"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"03edf5be-5871-4a12-bb08-4d910fd8dbf4"},"task_id":"03edf5be-5871-4a12-bb08-4d910fd8dbf4","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"03edf5be-5871-4a12-bb08-4d910fd8dbf4","chunk":"Read text file `/tmp/brev/boundary.md`.\n1|# TASK-260830-3bkz0c — shared-environment implementation boundary\n2|\n3|## Deliverable\n4|\n5|New package `internal/environ`: the single environment library\n6|behind the Provider, Session Adapter, and Directory Node\n7|facades (AX v0.5.0 §§7.8–7.9, 13.14, 10.8), plus the boundary\n8|battery that fails when the facades diverge.\n9|\n10|Production (`internal/environ/`, 4 files, new):\n11|- `decode.go` — `DecodeStrictObject` + `Fault` (UTF-8 / lone\n12|  surrogate / non-object / duplicate / trailing), string-walk\n13|  `HasLoneSurrogateEscape`, rune `StringLength` /\n14|  `CheckStringBounds`, uint53/digest/UUIDv7/timestamp bridges,\n15|  reverse-DNS extensions, sorted-unique helpers.\n16|- `tuple.go` — environment-id grammar, SemVer, amd64|arm64\n17|  table, exact six-member `DecodeTuple` (no extensions, no\n18|  executable provenance).\n19|- `observation.go` — `DecodeEnvironmentObservation` (§10.8.1,\n20|  reusing the tuple admission model), exact eight-name\n21|  capability map with reason-coherence in both directions.\n22|- `doc.go` — ownership and stated bounds.\n23|\n24|Battery (`internal/environ/`, 7 test files, 18 top-level tests,\n25|129 subtests, all green): implementation census + grammar\n26|one-language gate, frame-agreement matrix (5 judges), rune/byte\n27|measure battery, tuple agreement + member-table equality,\n28|observation battery + shared-table pins, identity agreement +\n29|member-table equality. Frozen `sessadapter`/`dirnode`\n30|production code untouched (no such files in the diff).\n31|\n32|## AC coverage: 7 of 7 rows driven through production entries\n33|\n34|| # | AC row | Production call site | Named test |\n35||---|---|---|---|\n36|| 1 | One environment library; census forbids new copies | `environ.DecodeStrictObject` (internal/environ/decode.go) | TestSharedImplementationsAreCensused |\n37|| 2 | Shared fixtures drive every facade | `sessadapter.DecodeTuple`, `dirnode.CheckScanRequest`, `provhost.DecodeManifest/CheckIdentity/DecodeSpawnPlan`, `canonicaljson.Canonicalize/CalculateObjectIdentity` | all battery files via corpus_test.go builders |\n38|| 3 | Shared identity | `provhost.CheckIdentity` (identity.go:102) vs `canonicaljson.CalculateObjectIdentity` (canonical.go:251) | TestIdentityAgreementAcrossValidators, TestIdentityProviderEqualityIsCallerRule |\n39|| 4 | Exact contract fixtures pass | `environ.DecodeTuple`, `environ.DecodeEnvironmentObservation` | valid rows in tuple/observation/identity/frame batteries |\n40|| 5 | Negative/refusal cases with full rendering | same entries as 2–4 | every refusal row asserts the rule phrase in the refusal text |\n41|| 6 | Crash/idempotency where durable state mutates | BOUND: pure validators, no store/cache (dirnode scan journal stays frozen leaf-2 scope) | TestEntriesAreDeterministic |\n42|| 7 | No unsupported capability advertised | `environ.DecodeEnvironmentObservation` (observation.go) — exact-eight map, unknown/ninth-key refusal; package exports no registry | ninth_capability_refused, unknown_capability_key, TestDirectoryCapabilityTableIsShared |\n43|\n44|## Live divergences found (recorded as ledger rows, fail closed either way)\n45|\n46|1. sessadapter+dirnode raw-scan surrogate gates REFUSE wire\n47|   bodies carrying literal backslash-u text (`\\\\ud800`);\n48|   environ+provhost+canonicaljson string-walk gates ACCEPT.\n49|   Proven via `DecodeTuple` / `CheckScanRequest` /\n50|   `Canonicalize`. sessadapter's\n51|   `TestSurrogateGateAgreesWithCanonicalJSON` is one-directional\n52|   and hides exactly this class.\n53|2. Truncated/malformed escapes refuse at the surrogate arm in\n54|   sessadapter/dirnode but at the syntax arm in\n55|   environ/provhost (same verdict, different arm).\n56|3. Wrong identity schema/version refuses at the member arm in\n57|   provhost but at the dispatch registry in canonicaljson (same\n58|   verdict, different arm).\n59|4. Provider equality is a caller rule (provhost refuses\n60|   invalid_config; canonicalizer accepts content) — by design,\n61|   ledgered in TestIdentityProviderEqualityIsCallerRule.\n62|\n63|Genuinely-required frozen-package change (not made):\n64|unifying sessadapter/dirnode on string-walk surrogate\n65|semantics requires editing their `hasLoneSurrogateEscape`\n66|implementations; both files are byte-frozen for this leaf, so\n67|the divergence is ledgered and the battery reddens on any\n68|unrecorded change in either direction.\n69|\n70|## Mutants: applied 7, killed 7 (narrowing 6/6, survivors none)\n71|\n72|N1 low-arm drop → bare_low_escape; N2 byte measure →\n73|environ_helper; N3 tuple extensions → extensions_refused; N4\n74|`!=`→`<` capabilities → ninth_capability_refused; N6 env-id\n75|`_` → TestSharedGrammarsAreOneLanguage; T1 token-preserving\n76|raw-scan rewrite (census still passes) → the 5\n77|escaped-backslash rows. D1 delete-only killed (existence only,\n78|excluded from the narrowing claim). Full log:\n79|`.temp/TASK-260830-3bkz0c/mutation-log.md`. Tree verified\n80|byte-identical after the battery (pre/post sha diff empty).\n81|\n82|## Gates (all exit 0, run directly, no pipes)\n83|\n84|- `go test ./... -count=1` — all 19 packages ok\n85|- `go test ./internal/environ/ -race -count=1` — ok\n86|- `go test ./internal/environ/ -cover -count=1` — 76.1%\n87|- `go vet ./...` and `GOOS=windows go vet ./...` — clean\n88|- `gofmt -l internal/` — clean\n89|- `go run ./internal/traceability/cmd/tracecheck` — ok\n90|  (contracts=60 sections=36), no ownership changes needed\n91|- `go generate ./internal/catalog` — no diff; `go build ./...` — ok\n92|\n93|## Bounds\n94|\n95|- Identity refusal dialects stay in provhost/canonicaljson\n96|  (agreement-pinned, not triplicated); byte-counted exec rules\n97|  stay in provhost §5.1 (ledgered, 3/3 byte gates driven);\n98|  tuple-registry signature/sequence/publication rules await the\n99|  registry owner; censuses of config/cliresult/terminalbackend/\n100|  axerror copies belong to their stories (scan scope stated in\n101|  census_test.go). No README/traceability edits: tracecheck is\n102|  green without them and both files have in-flight orchestrator\n103|  modifications I did not entangle."}}}
