y map) | ninth capability | TestDecodeEnvironmentObservation/ninth_capability_refused | KILLED |\n19|| N6 `n6_envunderscore.py`: env-id grammar admits `_` | underscore ids | TestSharedGrammarsAreOneLanguage | KILLED |\n20|| T1 `t1_rawscan.py`: gate keeps its name and refusal texts but matches `\\u` byte pairs without consuming `\\\\` pairs (raw-scan semantics) | escaped-backslash text | TestFrameAgreementAcrossFacades/escaped_backslash_{high,low,pair}_run2, _in_member_name, _nested (5 rows); TestSharedImplementationsAreCensused still PASSES under T1 | KILLED |\n21|\n22|T1 is the token-preserving attack on the census source-text\n23|gate: the symbol `HasLoneSurrogateEscape` stays defined, so a\n24|grep-level gate would pass, while the behavioral suite fails on\n25|exactly the escaped-backslash class. Census + behavior are\n26|complementary by construction, not by assertion.\n27|\n28|## Existence-only (not accepted as narrowing evidence)\n29|\n30|| Mutant | What it proves | Result |\n31||---|---|---|\n32|| D1 `d1_deletegate.py`: remove the surrogate-gate call (gate absent) | gate exists | KILLED (bare_high/low, high-followed-by-non-low, run3 rows) — existence only, excluded from the narrowing claim |\n33|\n34|## Totals\n35|\n36|Applied 7, killed 7. Narrowing kills 6 of 6 (N1, N2, N3, N4,\n37|N6, T1). Census-only kills 0 (no census-only mutant run).\n38|Over-applied (mutant fails to apply): 0. Survivors: none.\n39|Every surviving-mutant bound is therefore vacuous; no bound\n40|needs stating."}}}
